    "do you offer financing?": "Yes, we offer financing and we have a credit application and a loan calculator online. REQUIRED: whenever financing comes up, END your reply by asking \"Would you like me to send you the pre-approval form?\" - always offer it, do not wait for them to ask. If they say yes, text them https://bobbysautollc.com/creditapp and tell them it's on the way; never read the URL out loud.",
    "do you accept trade-ins? (feel free to be as detailed as you like)": "Yes, we take trade-ins, and there's a Value Your Trade-In tool on our site. A firm number requires us to look at the vehicle in person.",
    "any dealership policies the ai should know? (ex: \"no deposits\" or \"prices are firm\")": "We are a family owned used car dealership. Fair prices, superior service, and treating customers right. FEES: we do not publish a documentation, title or tag fee. NEVER state a fee amount and never invent one. If a caller asks about fees or what the out-the-door price is, say the listed price is the vehicle price and any fees or taxes are gone over in person when they come in. PRICING: a couple of vehicles are listed without a price. For those, do NOT guess or estimate - say we're pricing that one and invite them to come look at it or leave a number so someone can call them back with it. HOURS: we're open Monday through Friday, eight in the morning to six at night. SATURDAY IS BY APPOINTMENT ONLY - if a caller wants to come in on a Saturday, tell them Saturdays are appointment only and book them a specific time. We're closed Sunday, so never offer a Sunday slot. SERVICE DEPARTMENT: we're not just sales - we do full automotive service. Oil changes, brakes, engines, transmissions, diagnostics and front-end work, with current diagnostic equipment and skilled technicians. If someone calls about service or a repair, say we can help and take their name, number and what the vehicle is doing so the service side can call them back to schedule. Do not quote repair prices or estimates over the phone, and do not promise a turnaround time. TEST DRIVES: a valid driver's license and proof of insurance are required. Most of our vehicles are older, higher-mileage, budget-friendly cars - that's what we do. Never apologize for the mileage; talk about what the vehicle is good for. If a caller asks for a vehicle history report, say we'll go through it together at the lot rather than promising one over the phone.",
